      {
        "block_id": "block_000067",
        "block_index": 67,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Tips for buying organic",
        "text_sha256": "6223c85a6b1535e50e722ef289dd48dd6880bd83d79f0fb5e21cf974b0453890",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000068",
        "block_index": 68,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Here's how to get the best nutritional bang for your buck on organic items:",
        "text_sha256": "6be4582814e886dcfd6d326af07e4a5052379542e7f6bb5f5662e97f4cbef598",
        "word_count": 14
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000069",
        "block_index": 69,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Check out organic coupon sites and follow local health food stores on social media.",
        "text_sha256": "336bfd9146f01d6c33b145c1ba491bd811f622636b6000a6edd023735b784b76",
        "word_count": 14
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000070",
        "block_index": 70,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "When organic items are on sale, buy double the amount and freeze the leftovers. You can also head straight to the freezer aisle and stock up on frozen organic foods for less.",
        "text_sha256": "3db067f0872f75afbc744686ea3250be9a28c4f6ee90184a0c2fa84ad2586a7a",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000071",
        "block_index": 71,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Look for deals on organic foods, not only in local grocery stores but also in big-box stores.",
        "text_sha256": "f041deefdf61b1f9224c042b36651efc3566d133be016e9b21bde95367aa6aa7",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000072",
        "block_index": 72,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Skip the pre-wash and pre-cut organic items; when the work is done for you, it makes already-expensive organic foods even more expensive. So instead of buying organic baby carrots, buy organic regular size carrots for half the price and do the washing and cutting yourself.",
        "text_sha256": "09ba6d17a66f49bb9c6bffb7b484b868858f7d9df6dfbab27d00571e09c98217",
        "word_count": 45
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000073",
        "block_index": 73,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Choose store brands that say \"organic\" on the main label. If it says \"organic,\" it needs to follow the organic guidelines in the USDA organic certification program.",
        "text_sha256": "305ff92450b7937143738f3b3defac76a4164ce3077dd0c1a26b935a0110a9ef",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000074",
        "block_index": 74,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The bottom line: You can certainly opt for organic produce during pregnancy when it's practical, but remember that what's most important is choosing a wide variety of fresh, ripe fruits and veggies in a range of colors. What to Expect Community parent ValerianDusk says she adds some good-for-you veggies to her eggs to up the nutrition factor: \"I scramble 2 eggs, add spinach, peppers, pepper jack cheese, [and] seasoning, and throw it all together. Then I add hot sauce!”",
        "text_sha256": "42ac3caf48c842e07829bb03967bdbc1a8ac9fcf6356c9217dba80275cd58852",
        "word_count": 79
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000075",
        "block_index": 75,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "ValerianDusk says she adds some good-for-you veggies to her eggs to up the nutrition factor: \"I scramble 2 eggs, add spinach, peppers, pepper jack cheese, [and] seasoning, and throw it all together. Then I add hot sauce!”",
        "text_sha256": "1e8921f05557d0ad5dcbadf157f4b9dd9a9ad6a3199ac7a33e7ddb8942c727b7",
        "word_count": 37
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000076",
        "block_index": 76,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "And never assume that organic means completely safe. Though it won't be treated with most traditional synthetic pesticides, organic foods do still use organic pesticides and can still have bacteria like salmonella in them. So whether you buy organic or conventional, remember to fully cook your meat, poultry, and fish and wash your produce thoroughly before eating it.",
        "text_sha256": "6522368ea17564cd726e70cb13d543f11cbd7b7420753c78a0120caf3ea20c5e",
        "word_count": 58
      }
    ],
